menu "PlantHub BLE Collector"

config PLANTHUB_BLE_SCAN_ITVL_MS
    int "BLE scan interval (ms)"
    default 200
    help
        Time between scan window starts. Larger interval = more airtime for WiFi.

config PLANTHUB_BLE_SCAN_WINDOW_MS
    int "BLE scan window (ms)"
    default 60 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5
    default 80
    help
        Active listen time per interval. The C5 (single core, shared radio)
        defaults lower to keep the web UI responsive (PlanV1 3.1).

        The C6 deliberately has NO arm here and takes the generic 80. Its
        correct value is a radio-coexistence question, and the C3's 60 was
        measured on a chip whose WiFi was independently unreliable under
        BLE load (66% packet loss, HTTP wedging under request bursts).
        Copying that number to a different radio would be cargo cult. The
        M6a hardware gate measures C6 coexistence explicitly; set an arm
        here from that number, not before it.

endmenu
